{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T11:16:26.633Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both verifies pass.\n\n**Summary of what I did:**\n\n- **`src/core/vcs/snapshot.ts`** (new): `captureSnapshot` reads HEAD commit/branch, index digest, stash list, and status through the `Vcs` port, hashing every status-listed file (null for deletions). `compareSnapshots` yields `moved` (`head`/`branch`/`index`/`stash`) and the sorted changed files. It never runs git.\n- **`src/watcher/git-guard.ts`** (new): `beginGitGuard` selects via `selectVcs`, returns null under `NoVcs`, and captures before spawn; `check` captures after exit and appends one `vcs_violation` and, when warranted, one `scope_violation` (changed files outside the post-exit resolved scope and the change folder), logging a warning for each. Failed reads log and record nothing.\n- **`src/watcher/runner.ts`**: one import, `const gitGuard = await beginGitGuard(...)` right before `spawnTaskAgent`, and `await gitGuard?.check()` right after, before the `ok` test.\n- **`src/harness/types.ts`**: added `vcs_violation`/`scope_violation` event types and their payload interfaces in `OsqEventData`.\n- **`tests/vcs-guard.test.ts`** (new): 8 tests through `runWatcherOnce` in temp git repos with an acting fake adapter, covering all five git-state scenarios, all three scope scenarios, and the proposal's commit-and-land scenario.\n\n**Notable deviation:** `tests/import-graph.test.ts` caps `runner.ts` at strictly under 200 lines (baseline 199), so I compressed the adjacent `spawnTaskAgent` call to spread the existing `verifyCtx` object (behavior-preserving); `runner.ts` is now 193 lines.\n\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/vcs-guard.test.ts` → 8/8 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → exit 0 (typechecks, UI build, full suite, lint)"}}
